<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were at the following levels, with week-ago and year-ago levels, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>			26/9/96		  19/9/96	     28/9/95</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    425			475		   450</p>
<p>    Naphtha		50		    25-50		    75</p>
<p>    Gas oil   1,500-1,525		    1,550		 2,050</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	275-300			300	     450-475</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     15			 15		 20-25</p>
<p>Motor gasoline stocks dipped as open arbitrage to the U.S. allowed transatlantic shipments.</p>
<p>Naphtha inventories rose slightly as incoming coasters outweighed feedstock outgoings to the German petchem industry.</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks fell with material heading for the normal heating oil markets. Product also arrived, then left after being blended to IPE standard.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories also dipped with German straight-run and ARA bunker demand.</p>
<p>Jet fuel stocks were steady, despite some product entering the gas oil pool for blending.</p>
<p>-- Philip Blenkinsop, Amsterdam Newsroom, 31 20 504 5004</p>
